  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "misir-wat"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Misir Wat"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is one of the most common dishes on an Ethiopian injera platter. Red lentils cook quickly and soak up a blend of chilli, cumin and turmeric without any fuss. The result is a thick, vivid stew that is hearty enough to eat as a main course."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The key is frying the spices in a little oil before adding the lentils. This wakes them up and gives the finished stew a much deeper flavour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
