      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oil in a large saucepan over medium heat. Add the onions and cook for 12 minutes, stirring often, until soft and lightly golden."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the garlic, ginger, chilli flakes, paprika, coriander, cumin and turmeric. Stir for 2 minutes until fragrant. Add the tomato puree and cook for a further minute."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the rinsed lentils and pour in the water. Stir well to combine. Bring to the boil."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Reduce the heat to low and simmer uncovered for 20 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the lentils are completely soft and the stew is thick. Add a little more water if it becomes too dry before the lentils are cooked."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Taste and adjust chilli. Serve on injera or with rice. A small drizzle of good vegetable oil on top is traditional."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Lentils are still firm after 20 minutes"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add another 100 ml of water and continue simmering. Old dried lentils can take longer. Rinse them before cooking but there is no need to soak red lentils."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Stew is watery"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Simmer uncovered over medium heat for 5 to 10 more minutes. The lentils will continue to absorb liquid as the stew cools."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "issue": "Flavour is bland"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Increase the chilli flakes and add another teaspoon of paprika. The spices need to fry before the lentils go in to bloom properly."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ethiopian Orthodox Christians fast for over 200 days a year, avoiding meat and animal products. Misir Wat fills that gap on the table. It is eaten across all regions of the country. It always appears alongside other vegetable stews on a shared platter. Lentils are among the oldest cultivated crops in East Africa."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
